course: dictionary
lesson: 8466
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Salmon is one of them: it can be a fish, the food made from that fish, or a colour. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: «Fish have many more small bones than mammals, such as the thin pin bones in salmon.» Fish have bones, so here salmon means the fish itself. Always ask: which meaning would make sense in this sentence?
explain: «Most salmon eaten in Britain comes from fish farms.» The word eaten is the clue. You cannot eat a whole fish swimming in the sea, so here salmon means the pink food. In a phrase like «salmon pink», salmon is a colour.
fact: A salmon is a large silver fish that lives in the sea but swims up rivers to lay its eggs.
fact: Salmon is also the pink flesh of this fish, which people eat as food.
fact: Salmon can also mean an orange-pink colour, as in «salmon pink».
fact: In science, the salmon's life cycle is famous: it is born in a river, grows up in the sea, and swims back upstream, even jumping waterfalls, to lay eggs where it was born.
fact: Salmon is a healthy food, with fats that are good for the brain.
exercise: «Wild salmon swim up rivers to lay their eggs.» In this sentence, what is a salmon? | *A large silver fish | An orange-pink colour | The pink flesh eaten as food | A river
exercise: «We had smoked salmon on toast for lunch.» What is salmon in this sentence? | *The pink flesh of the fish, eaten as food | A colour like a sunset | A fish that lives only in rivers | A sea bird
exercise: Which phrase uses salmon to mean a colour, not a fish? | tinned salmon | *salmon pink | smoked salmon | salmon run
test: «Fish have many more small bones than mammals, such as the thin pin bones in salmon.» Here salmon means what? | *A fish | A pink colour | A river | Food from a shop
test: Which of these is a true fact about salmon? | Salmon has feathers like a robin | Salmon lives only in deserts | *A salmon swims back up rivers to lay its eggs where it was born | A salmon is a small brown bird
exam: In «Mia's dress was salmon pink», what does salmon mean? | *A colour | A fish | Food from the sea | A river
